# Milestone 14 (Production Infrastructure) — keeps the Docker build context
# (repo root — every Dockerfile here builds `docker build -f ... .`, per
# each Dockerfile's own header comment) small and, more importantly, never
# lets a real secret or a stale local build artifact leak into an image
# layer. `.env*` is the entry that matters most here: `apps/api/.env`
# holds real local credentials — COPY-ing it into an image (even
# transiently, in a layer nothing later strips) would bake a secret into
# every derived image and every layer-cache export of it.

# Dependency/build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image itself;
# copying a host copy in would use the WRONG platform's native binaries
# (a real, common Docker footgun) and defeats each Dockerfile's own
# layer-caching design (COPY manifests → RUN install → COPY source).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/generated

# Secrets — never send these to the Docker daemon/build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs/tests unrelated to what any image actually runs — smaller context,
# faster `docker build` upload, no effect on any image's own contents
# (nothing in these paths is COPY'd by any Dockerfile).
docs
infrastructure/terraform
infrastructure/k8s
infrastructure/observability
